    "created_at": "2023-01-23T09:14:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-01-23T09:15:17Z",
    "body": "As long as infra describes things to use in algorithms, I think this belongs there. After all, people are copying the style and usage across multiple specifications, and the point of infra is to help them do that appropriately. Relying on algorithms as a definitive normative explanation, when they are expressed in an undocumented format that allows for ambiguities, can have the effect of \"hiding\" those ambiguities behind an appearance of rigour.\r\n\r\n(I appreciate having algorithms, but I hope a best practices guide will include \"explain what happens in prose even if it's non-normative, instead of assuming that the algorithms are self-explanatory\". )",
    "author_association": "NONE",
